       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\nAcetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. This much acetaminophen risks serious liver injury, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n- **500\u20131000 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed**, not to exceed 3,000\u20134,000 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. Please also confirm it with your supervising resident or attending, as you would for any order."
      }
