       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen risks acute liver failure, and I'm not willing to place an order that could seriously harm the patient. You're also a student, so the order would need a licensed prescriber's review anyway.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If it was a typo,** give me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **If you think this dose is intended,** talk to your supervising resident, attending, or a pharmacist. A prescriber can enter it directly, and pharmacy will likely flag it.\n- **If the goal is stronger pain control,** I can help you think through options. These include scheduled acetaminophen at a safe dose plus an NSAID, if appropriate, or other analgesics. Your team would make the final decision.\n\nWhat would you like me to do?"
